WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
This is volume three and it's the first segment.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.700
We begin with November the first 1899, the purification of the Church.

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:16.700
Louisa says, "As I was in my usual state, I found myself outside of myself inside a church,

4
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.200
in which there was a priest celebrating the divine sacrifice,

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.300
and while doing this he was crying bitterly and said,

6
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.000
"The pillar of my church has no place to lean."

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.700
Now I don't know if you remember, back in the 12th century the Church had a crisis

8
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:37.500
and the pope at the time had a vision of a little man, literally tiny,

9
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:43.300
putting his shoulder to the church and some months later when he met Francis of Assisi

10
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:49.900
and his first companions, he recognized him as the small man that he had seen.

11
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.500
In the act in which Jesus was saying this, Louisa said, "I saw a pillar."

12
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.900
It's top touch the heavens and the bottom of this pillar at the bottom of it,

13
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.900
there were priests, bishops, cardinals and all the other dignities sustaining the pillar.

14
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.700
To my surprise, I went about looking and I saw that of all these people,

15
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.200
some were weak, some were half rotten, some were infirm and some full of mud.

16
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.200
Now that's a spiritual diagnosis, okay?

17
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.300
They were not like this on the outside, they were like this on the inside

18
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.300
and of course we're living at the stage where this has actually happened.

19
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:32.500
So very scarce was the number of those who were in a condition in which they could sustain it.

20
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.700
So this poor pillar kept swaying, unable to remain still,

21
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.900
so many were the quakes it received from the bottom because all the people at the bottom were in trouble.

22
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:49.400
At the top of this pillar there was the Holy Father, now in 1899 the Holy Father was Leo XIII

23
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.900
and you remember the great vision that Leo XIII got after Mass

24
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.900
in which he witnessed a dialogue between Jesus and Satan

25
00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:04.300
and Satan asked for 100 years to destroy the church and amazingly he got permission.

26
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:09.500
Of course he didn't get permission to destroy the church but to test it, to sift it like wheat.

27
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.200
Do you remember before the passion that Jesus said to Peter?

28
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:19.600
All of you will be sifted like wheat and it happened during the terrible passion of Jesus.

29
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.500
So at the top of this pillar there was the Holy Father who with gold chains

30
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.200
and with rays emanating from his whole person did as much as he could to sustain it.

31
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.900
Now that means that rays coming from his whole person means he's truly in grace

32
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:38.500
and to chain and illuminate the people who dwelled at the bottom the Holy Father did as much as he could.

33
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:44.500
Although some of them would flee so as to be more comfortable in being rotten and covered with mud.

34
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:50.700
Now in 1899 the atheistic materialism that had been launched on the world

35
00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.800
through the French Revolution had really taken hold

36
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:59.400
and it was about to spill out over the whole world in the 20th century

37
00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:06.700
and make 20th century what Jesus himself calls the most evil and violent of all centuries.

38
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.900
So let me just read that a little bit again.

39
00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.300
The Holy Father did as much as he could to stop people at the bottom from doing bad

40
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.900
and to illuminate them that is with his teachings and his prayers and everything.

41
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.100
But they ran away from him in order to enjoy becoming rotten

42
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.200
and to enjoy being covered with mud.

43
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.000
In other words they enjoyed the heresies they were going into.

44
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.700
And not only this but he did as much as he could to bind and to illuminate the whole world.

45
00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.800
Now bind is to bind them to the truth, to illuminate is to teach them properly.

46
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:43.900
So in other words to put this very very simply she saw a crisis in the clergy and the hierarchy.

47
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.400
We're in the depths of that crisis now.

48
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.500
While I was seeing this that priesthood was celebrating Mass.

49
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.700
I'm not sure whether he was a priest or the Lord Louisa said.

50
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.000
It seems to me that it was Jesus but I cannot tell with certainty.

51
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.900
He called me close to himself and he said my daughter.

52
00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.700
Now if she's addressed as my daughter was definitely Jesus.

53
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.800
See in what heart-rending state my church is.

54
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:15.200
Now in these writings Louisa usually sees that when she sees Jesus in a terrible state during his passion.

55
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.400
Because he's now in glory of course and he's not suffering.

56
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.200
But his mystical body on earth is suffering.

57
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.200
And so when he would want her to appreciate what was going on in the church

58
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.000
she would see him in some aspect of being crucified.

59
00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.800
So he says in what a heart-rending state my church is.

60
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:39.000
The very ones who were supposed to sustain her withdrawal and with their works they knock her down.

61
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.200
They beat her and they reach the point of even denigrating her.

62
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:49.000
That means they've gone off into this atheistic Marxism and materialism and modernism

63
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.400
and all the stuff hope I asked the tenth a few years after this actually condemned.

64
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:58.800
The only remedy is that I cause so much blood to be shed.

65
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.700
That's the blood of martyrs usually.

66
00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:06.100
As to form a bath to wash away that rotten mud and to heal their deep wounds.

67
00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:10.000
Now what he's saying here is something you already know.

68
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.600
And that is that the blood of the martyrs actually cleanses the church.

69
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.900
Just as his blood brought about not only the cleansing of the world but brought about redemption itself.

70
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:23.600
So the martyrs then participate in a very deep way in redemption.

71
00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:29.700
He said so I cause so much blood to be shed as to form a bath to wash away that rotten mud

72
00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:35.400
and to heal their deep wounds so that healed, strengthened and embellished in that blood.

73
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:41.200
They may become instruments capable of keeping the church stable and firm.

74
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:48.000
Then he added I have called you to tell you do you want to be a victim soul.

75
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Now my book simply says a victim but in our day and age you cannot leave that word by itself.

76
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.200
It will be misunderstood.

77
00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:59.800
Do you want to be a victim soul and therefore be like a prop to sustain this pillar in these times.

78
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.000
So incorrigible.

79
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.800
So he is calling Louisa to accept the role of being a victim soul.

80
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.900
And therefore she would stand between the justice of God and the sinfulness of man.

81
00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:19.000
Holding back some of the justice of God in order to have as many people as possible saved like all of the mystics.

82
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.800
She won't succeed completely.

83
00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:28.200
But she will succeed somewhat and this is the story that we're going to be dealing with as we go through all of these volumes.

84
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:33.500
So Louisa said at first a shiver ran through me for fear that I might not have the strength.

85
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.000
But then immediately I offered myself and I pronounced the fiat.

86
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.200
Now beside that I want you to put John 15 5 without me Jesus says you can do nothing.

87
00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.400
So you can definitely say yes to this because it won't be yourself.

88
00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.300
It'll be the Lord.

89
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:54.900
So with that I want to give you Philippians for 13, but I can do all things in Christ who gives me the strength, which is a different matter altogether.

90
00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.100
So Louisa said her yes or fear at that moment.

91
00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:07.000
I found myself surrounded by many saints angels and purging souls as the souls in purgatory who tormented me with scourges and other instruments.

92
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:13.300
In other words, immediately began to give her the experience of making reparation for the church.

93
00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:18.500
At first I felt a certain fear and then the more I suffered, the more I wanted to suffer.

94
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:25.100
And I enjoyed the suffering like a most sweet nectar more so since the thought touched me.

95
00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:31.400
Now when she says that she enjoyed the suffering, no human being enjoys suffering.

96
00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:35.600
So you've got to put Hebrews 12 to beside that.

97
00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:44.500
Now Hebrews 12 to says that for the joy that was set before him, he endured the cross despising the shame of it.

98
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:52.500
So you endure the suffering and the reason why you're happy to endure the suffering is that you appreciate what it's doing.

99
00:07:52.500 --> 00:08:04.300
In other words, as we go through these volumes, you will realize that suffering voluntarily for love of God has an enormous value in the eyes of God and he calls it divine currency.

100
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:11.200
And it's with this divine currency that you can, if I can use the word buy with inverted commas, you can buy souls.

101
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:18.700
In other words, you can pay part of their redemption or you can participate in Jesus's redemption because Jesus said,

102
00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.700
I am divine and you are my branches.

103
00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:26.000
So if he's the Redeemer, then we are to be core redeemers because we're branches of that vine.

104
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.900
And that's why he calls us into this wonderful mission of the divine will.

105
00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.700
It's definitely not a devotion.

106
00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:40.700
It's a mission in which we enter into being core redeemers with Christ to the depths that you want to go to.

107
00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.700
The Lord will never push you.

108
00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:47.100
So she said she felt a fear first and then she was happy and then the thought came to her.

109
00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:54.400
Who knows whether these pains might be the means to consume my life so that I might take wing in the last flight towards my only good.

110
00:08:54.400 --> 00:09:01.000
Now, one of the totally extraordinary things about Louisa is her extraordinary desire to go to heaven.

111
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.800
Now, it's not a desire to die as such.

112
00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.700
In other words, I want to get rid of this earth.

113
00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:07.900
I want to get rid of this body.

114
00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.500
That's the way suicides think.

115
00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:12.100
That's not Louisa's situation.

116
00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:15.000
Louisa wants to die because she has seen the Lord.

117
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.900
She has seen heaven and she will see it an awful lot more as we go along in the volumes as well.

118
00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:26.900
And the more she gets to know the Lord and the more she loves him, the more she wants to go and be with the Lord.

119
00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:37.300
So for that, I want to give you two Corinthians 5 verses 1 to 10, where Saint Paul also says that he would like to throw off the veil of the flesh and go to the Lord.

120
00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.600
But he would stay on on the earth to fulfill his mission out of love for God.

121
00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.200
And it's exactly what the Lord asks Louisa to do.

122
00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:56.700
So, but to my highest sorrow, Louisa said, after suffering bitter pains, I saw that these pains would not consume my life and that this fragile flesh prevents me from uniting myself to the eternal good.

123
00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:05.800
So she began to realize rather quickly that she could suffer all of this agony, but it was not going to take her life because that wasn't God's will.

124
00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:13.100
For her, God's will was that she would suffer on the earth as he suffered on the earth to save souls on the earth as he did.

125
00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:20.400
So, Louisa said, after this, I saw the bloody slaughter that was made of the people who were at the bottom of the pillar.

126
00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.000
What a horrible catastrophe.

127
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:32.000
Now, once the Lord gives information to his saints or to his prophets, I want to give you Amos 3-7.

128
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.500
The Lord never does anything without telling the saints first, without telling the prophets.

129
00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:39.500
That's what they call the saints in the Old Testament.

130
00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.800
And here in Louisa sees a terrible slaughter.

131
00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:55.500
Now, from about 2017, I think we had the terrible Soviet Union catastrophe starting with the Bolshevik Revolution and that literally millions of people died as a result of that.

132
00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:01.300
And communism had a terrible victory there and the church received the most dreadful persecution there.

133
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.300
So it could be that.

134
00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:10.700
But our lady in Fatima comes in 2017 and she tells us that if we don't repent, there will be a terrible slaughter.

135
00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:18.500
Now, before both of those events that I've just said, you have the First World War, 1914 to 1918.

136
00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:22.300
So, she's seeing ahead of time the terrible war.

137
00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:28.300
Now, you know that the First World War was called the war to end all wars, but it ended nothing.

138
00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:35.500
We had an even worse one, 1939 to '45, and there is a Third World War being cooked up at the moment as well,

139
00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:45.000
which will be even infinitely worse, partly because the instruments they have devised for killing are much more technical and they're much more efficient.

140
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.000
So you don't even have to send an army anymore.

141
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:55.700
You can send a missile across the world and you can send it and destroy a whole nation absolutely without them knowing what is coming.

142
00:11:55.700 --> 00:12:02.000
So Louisa said, "So very scarce was the number of those who would not be victims."

143
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.000
That is in this terrible catastrophe.

144
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.400
They reached such daringness as to try and kill the Holy Father as well.

145
00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:12.700
Well, that's true. They made a prisoner in the Vatican of the Holy Father as well.

146
00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:23.000
But then it seemed to me that that blood which was shed and those bloody tormented victims were the means to render those who remained strong,

147
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.600
so as to sustain the pillar without letting it sway anymore.

148
00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:34.100
So the people who survived these terrible wars were the ones whose faith was renewed and who supported the Church.

149
00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:38.100
After this, she said, "Days of triumphs and of peace would arise."

150
00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:43.400
And of course, we've had a so-called "peace" since the Second World War.

151
00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:47.200
Not really because there's been wars all over the place, but they call it peace anyway.

152
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.800
But this is not the triumph of the mekulate heart that our mother spoke about.

153
00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.800
And it's not the triumph of the Sacred Heart that Jesus spoke about.

154
00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.900
That is still to come.

155
00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.900
So there will be days of triumphs and of peace will arise.

156
00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:05.700
The face of the earth seemed to be renewed and the pillar would acquire its original prestige and splendor.

157
00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:15.300
Now, this is very early in Louisa's work, but we now know that after the Third World War, the terrible chastisement that's coming,

158
00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:23.800
there will be the new era of the new and divine holiness which the Lord will ask Louisa to actually open the door for this to happen.

159
00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:31.100
And there will be a period of most wonderful grace and peace on the earth before the final onslaught of Satan.

160
00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:40.400
"Oh, happy days," she said, "I hail you from afar, days which will give great glory to my church and great honor to the God who is her head."

161
00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:45.600
So Louisa is seeing something in the far distant future, even for you and me.

162
00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:51.300
So November the 3rd, 1899, Jesus enjoys himself with Louisa.

163
00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:54.700
Now, my book uses the word amusement or amuses.

164
00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:59.700
Now, we don't use that language, so I want to change it to "enjoys" which we do use.

165
00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:03.700
In other words, people who love each other play little love games with each other.

166
00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:09.000
So this morning, my beloved Jesus came and transported me outside of myself inside a church.

167
00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.700
And then he disappeared and I was left alone.

168
00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:16.700
Now, finding myself in the presence of the most blessed sacrament, I did my usual adoration.

169
00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:24.300
But while I was doing this, it seemed to have become all eyes to see whether I would catch the sight of Jesus.

170
00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:29.700
At that moment, I saw him on the altar as a child calling me with his gracious little hand.

171
00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.400
Who could say my contentment?

172
00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:34.300
I flew to him, she said, without thinking of anything else.

173
00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:37.200
I clasped him in my arms and I kissed him.

174
00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:43.700
But in the action which I was doing this, he assumed a serious appearance showing that he did not like my kisses.

175
00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:48.100
And he began to reject me, heedless of this, I continued and I said to him,

176
00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.900
"My pretty little one, beautiful one.

177
00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:55.200
The other day you wanted to pour yourself out with me with kisses and with hugs, and I gave you all the freedom.

178
00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.100
Today, I too want to pour myself out with you."

179
00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:01.000
This is the tit-for-tat of the love games.

180
00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.100
"Oh, please give me the freedom to do it, but he continued to reject me."

181
00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:07.900
And in seeing that I wouldn't stop, he disappeared.

182
00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:13.500
Who can say how mortified and concerned I was left when I found myself inside of myself?

183
00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.700
However, after a little while, he came back.

184
00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:21.200
And as I wanted to ask him for forgiveness for what my book calls "impertenances".

185
00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:26.800
Now, impertenances cannot be the correct translation because impertinence is sinful.

186
00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.300
It's sinful behavior.

187
00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:34.700
So, I want you to change that word to boldness because she said she was daring up above, okay?

188
00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.300
I wanted to ask him forgiveness for my boldness.

189
00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:40.800
He forgave me by wanting to pour himself out with me.

190
00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:48.200
And while kissing me, he said, "Beloved of my heart, my divinity resides in you habitually."

191
00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:53.700
Now, the blessed trinity was given to us in baptism to abide in us.

192
00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:58.000
But it only stays with us when we're in grace, 1 Corinthians 3, 16.

193
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:03.500
No, you not that you are the temple of the living God and that God dwells in you.

194
00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:08.000
So, when Jesus says that my divinity resides in you habitually,

195
00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:14.600
he's speaking about the level of grace that she has because in Volume 2,

196
00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:18.200
we were told that Jesus said, "I am grace.

197
00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:20.400
Grace is an outpouring of God himself."

198
00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:23.200
So, if we have this outpouring of God in us,

199
00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.500
naturally, he will find it easy to stay with us.

200
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.600
So, "Beloved of my heart, my divinity resides in you habitually.

201
00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:34.600
And just as you keep inventing new things to make me delight with you,

202
00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:38.200
so I give you tit for tat, because see, these are love games.

203
00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:41.000
I use new ways to make you delight with me.

204
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.800
With this, I understood that it had been a joke.

205
00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.300
My book says, "God never jokes with us.

206
00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:49.600
It had been a game that Jesus wanted to play."

207
00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:53.800
Because you see, he came towards a child and children play.

208
00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:58.800
