and that is that the authority given by Jesus

433
00:32:08.800 --> 00:32:11.800
to the priesthood in the church is real.

434
00:32:11.800 --> 00:32:14.800
So real that if the priest says, "Aegotai absolvey,"

435
00:32:14.800 --> 00:32:16.800
God absolves you from your sins.

436
00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:19.800
If the priest says, "This is my body, and this is my blood,"

437
00:32:19.800 --> 00:32:22.800
under the right conditions and properly ordained,

438
00:32:22.800 --> 00:32:27.800
then the Lord does, in fact, come and become Eucharist for us.

439
00:32:27.800 --> 00:32:29.800
That's just to give you two examples.

440
00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:32.800
If the priest says, "I baptize you in the name of the Father,"

441
00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:35.800
you are baptized in the name of the Father, and that's it.

442
00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:36.800
That's the priestly authority.

443
00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:41.800
Now, what you find is that God acknowledges that priestly authority.

444
00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:47.800
Regardless of whether the man who is the priest is worthy of that authority or not,

445
00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:50.800
this is something that has to be clarified in the age that you and I live in

446
00:32:50.800 --> 00:32:54.800
in which the hierarchy and the clergy are in crisis.

447
00:32:54.800 --> 00:32:56.800
Their authority is to be respected.

448
00:32:56.800 --> 00:32:59.800
The individual person may or may not be worthy of that.

449
00:32:59.800 --> 00:33:06.800
Now, exorcists will also tell you that the demon recognizes priestly authority.

450
00:33:06.800 --> 00:33:10.800
There's a very wonderful example in the Acts of the Apostles

451
00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:13.800
where the sons of Skiva, seven sons of Skiva,

452
00:33:13.800 --> 00:33:19.800
were trying to cast out demons in the name of Jesus whom Paul knows about.

453
00:33:19.800 --> 00:33:21.800
Now, they didn't believe in Jesus,

454
00:33:21.800 --> 00:33:24.800
but they knew that Paul was working in credible miracles.

455
00:33:24.800 --> 00:33:28.800
And so the demon says, "Who do you think you are?

456
00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:34.800
I know this Jesus, and I know this Paul, and he attacked them and nearly destroyed them."

457
00:33:34.800 --> 00:33:41.800
Any of our exorcists, which, of course, has to be priests properly appointed by bishops,

458
00:33:41.800 --> 00:33:42.800
to do an exorcism.

459
00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:45.800
I don't mean a deliverance now, I mean an exorcism.

460
00:33:45.800 --> 00:33:49.800
The demon will recognize the authority of the priest,

461
00:33:49.800 --> 00:33:53.800
but if somebody pretends to have that authority, the demon will just attack them.

462
00:33:53.800 --> 00:33:56.800
That's just a good lesson on priestly authority.

463
00:33:56.800 --> 00:34:00.800
So let's come to November the 11th, 1899.

464
00:34:00.800 --> 00:34:03.800
Obedience prevents her from conforming to justice.

465
00:34:03.800 --> 00:34:06.800
Obedience means she gets an order from the priesthood.

466
00:34:06.800 --> 00:34:09.800
As I was in my usual state, Louise has said,

467
00:34:09.800 --> 00:34:13.800
"I found myself outside of myself, and it seemed I was going around the earth.

468
00:34:13.800 --> 00:34:18.800
Oh, how inundated it was with all sorts of iniquities."

469
00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:20.800
It's horrifying to think about it.

470
00:34:20.800 --> 00:34:26.800
Now, while going around, I arrived at some place where I found a priest of holy life,

471
00:34:26.800 --> 00:34:30.800
and in another place, a virgin of blameless and holy life.

472
00:34:30.800 --> 00:34:35.800
We gathered the three of us together, and we began to converse about the many chastisements

473
00:34:35.800 --> 00:34:39.800
that the Lord was sending, and about the many others that He keeps prepared.

474
00:34:39.800 --> 00:34:43.800
And I said to them, "And you, what do you do?

475
00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:46.800
Have you perhaps conformed to divine justice?"

476
00:34:46.800 --> 00:34:50.800
And they said, "Seeing the strict necessity of these times,

477
00:34:50.800 --> 00:34:54.800
and that man would not surrender even if an apostle came out,

478
00:34:54.800 --> 00:34:57.800
or if the Lord sent another Saint Vincent Ferrer,

479
00:34:57.800 --> 00:35:03.800
who might induce him to conversion with miracles and prodigious signs."

480
00:35:03.800 --> 00:35:08.800
On the contrary, seeing that man has reached such obstinacy

481
00:35:08.800 --> 00:35:14.800
and a sort of insanity, this is 1899, it's infinitely worse now.

482
00:35:14.800 --> 00:35:21.800
And a source of insanity that the very power of miracles would render him more incredulous.

483
00:35:21.800 --> 00:35:25.800
Actually, we've arrived at the stage that working a miracle would be a waste of time.

484
00:35:25.800 --> 00:35:27.800
Isn't it really sad?

485
00:35:27.800 --> 00:35:30.800
So when Jesus worked miracles at the time of the incarnation,

486
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:36.800
human beings were still at a level where, if God touched them, they would acknowledge it.

487
00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:41.800
But we've gone so far down the road that we wouldn't acknowledge it.

488
00:35:41.800 --> 00:35:47.800
We being the human race, not you and I as individuals.

489
00:35:47.800 --> 00:35:52.800
So this is the holy priest and the holy virgin speaking to Louisa.

490
00:35:52.800 --> 00:35:55.800
So invested by this most strict necessity,

491
00:35:55.800 --> 00:35:58.800
and for the good of men, that's the human race,

492
00:35:58.800 --> 00:36:02.800
in order to arrest this rotten sea that inundates the face of the earth,

493
00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:09.800
and for the glory of God so offended, we have conformed to justice.

494
00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:12.800
In other words, we agree what the Lord is doing.

495
00:36:12.800 --> 00:36:16.800
But we are praying and offering ourselves as victim souls

496
00:36:16.800 --> 00:36:20.800
so that these chastisements may turn out to be the conversion of the peoples.

497
00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:22.800
But you, what do you do?

498
00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:24.800
Have you conformed with us?

499
00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:29.800
And Louisa said, "I know, I can't because obedience doesn't want it."

500
00:36:29.800 --> 00:36:32.800
In other words, she's under strict obedience to the priest.

501
00:36:32.800 --> 00:36:36.800
Even though Jesus wants me to conform, but since obedience does not want it,

502
00:36:36.800 --> 00:36:40.800
obedience must prevail over everything.

503
00:36:40.800 --> 00:36:43.800
Now, Jesus will tell Louisa that that is correct,

504
00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:47.800
that no matter whose opinion wants to change her,

505
00:36:47.800 --> 00:36:52.800
that whatever is told to her in obedience, that is what she has to do.

506
00:36:52.800 --> 00:36:56.800
So I am forced to be always in contrast with Jesus, she said,

507
00:36:56.800 --> 00:36:58.800
which afflicts me very much, and they said,

508
00:36:58.800 --> 00:37:01.800
"Oh, when it's obedience, surely one must adhere."

509
00:37:01.800 --> 00:37:06.800
So when the priest and the holy woman hears that indeed it is obedience

510
00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:09.800
that is ordering her, then they verm for her,

511
00:37:09.800 --> 00:37:11.800
"Yes, you've got to obey."

512
00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:13.800
So after this finding myself inside of myself,

513
00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:16.800
I saw my dearest Jesus for just a little,

514
00:37:16.800 --> 00:37:19.800
and I wanted to know where that priest and the virgin came from,

515
00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:21.800
and he told me they were from Peru.

516
00:37:21.800 --> 00:37:29.800
So these suggested identities are Rose of Lima and Martin de Porres.

517
00:37:29.800 --> 00:37:33.800
If you know better, you can tell the rest of us.

518
00:37:33.800 --> 00:37:38.800
November 12th, 1899, Jesus allows Jesus to spare a chastisement,

519
00:37:38.800 --> 00:37:39.800
so he's going to be happy.

520
00:37:39.800 --> 00:37:44.800
This morning my beloved Jesus came and transported me outside of myself,

521
00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:49.800
and I saw as if something was supposed to move from the heavens to touch the earth.

522
00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:55.800
Now this is 1899, and in 1908 there was a meteor that struck Siberia,

523
00:37:55.800 --> 00:37:59.800
and obviously the victim's souls were really interceding,

524
00:37:59.800 --> 00:38:03.800
because it fell in a place where nobody was living,

525
00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:06.800
and therefore, while it did a lot of destruction,

526
00:38:06.800 --> 00:38:08.800
it didn't actually kill anybody.

527
00:38:08.800 --> 00:38:11.800
I was so frightened she said that I screamed,

528
00:38:11.800 --> 00:38:14.800
and I said to him, "Oh please, oh please Lord, what are you doing?

529
00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:16.800
How much ruin it will bring if this happens?"

530
00:38:16.800 --> 00:38:18.800
So she sees the meteor coming.

531
00:38:18.800 --> 00:38:21.800
And of course, a meteor can spell the end of an era,

532
00:38:21.800 --> 00:38:25.800
as it has done for the era of the dinosaurs and so on.

533
00:38:25.800 --> 00:38:30.800
So, Louisa continues, "How much ruin will come if this happens?

534
00:38:30.800 --> 00:38:34.800
You tell me that you love me, and then you want me to be so frightened."

535
00:38:34.800 --> 00:38:36.800
You have seen it, haven't you?

536
00:38:36.800 --> 00:38:38.800
No, don't do it, don't, no, no.

537
00:38:38.800 --> 00:38:41.800
You can't do it, because I don't want it.

538
00:38:41.800 --> 00:38:44.800
Now there you have the victim's soul telling the Lord,

539
00:38:44.800 --> 00:38:46.800
"No, I don't want it."

540
00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:50.800
That meteor did not strike any town.

541
00:38:50.800 --> 00:38:56.800
It struck in an area that was very far from where anybody was living.

542
00:38:56.800 --> 00:38:59.800
But everything in the area was destroyed.

543
00:38:59.800 --> 00:39:02.800
No, no, she said, "I don't want it."

544
00:39:02.800 --> 00:39:06.800
And Jesus, all compassion for me told me, "My daughter, don't fear."

545
00:39:06.800 --> 00:39:10.800
And then, "When have you ever wanted me to do anything?"

546
00:39:10.800 --> 00:39:12.800
He says to her, "You know, you're always preventing me."

547
00:39:12.800 --> 00:39:13.800
He's only teasing her.

548
00:39:13.800 --> 00:39:16.800
"I shouldn't let you see anything when I chastise people,

549
00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.800
otherwise you bind me everywhere."

550
00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:22.800
Well then, "I will fortify your heart," my book says,

551
00:39:22.800 --> 00:39:25.800
"I will strengthen your heart with fortitude."

552
00:39:25.800 --> 00:39:27.800
Now fortitude is the most wonderful gift of God.

553
00:39:27.800 --> 00:39:31.800
It's like the steel girders they put into the skyscrapers

554
00:39:31.800 --> 00:39:34.800
so that they can withstand even the hurricanes.

555
00:39:34.800 --> 00:39:39.800
So the hurricanes of the spiritual life can be handled with the gift of fortitude.

556
00:39:39.800 --> 00:39:43.800
I'll make as though a trunk rises from it, that's from your heart,

557
00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:46.800
so as to hold whatever you see still.

558
00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:49.800
And then I will pour so many graces on you

559
00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:52.800
that you'll be able to nourish myself and my children.

560
00:39:52.800 --> 00:39:56.800
Now, I want you to note that Jesus' word is creative.

561
00:39:56.800 --> 00:39:59.800
When he said, "Let there be light," there was light.

562
00:39:59.800 --> 00:40:02.800
When he said, "Let us make man in our own image and likeness,"

563
00:40:02.800 --> 00:40:03.800
that's what happened.

564
00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:07.800
When Jesus speaks to us, he also creates the reality inside of us.

565
00:40:07.800 --> 00:40:11.800
For example, if I needed to forgive somebody, thank God I don't,

566
00:40:11.800 --> 00:40:16.800
if I did, and Jesus said to me, forgive, he automatically gives me the grace

567
00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:18.800
and the courage to forgive.

568
00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:21.800
So it's a very big sin if I don't do it.

569
00:40:21.800 --> 00:40:26.800
So at that moment, Louisa said, something like a trunk did come out of my heart

570
00:40:26.800 --> 00:40:29.800
with two branches at the top in the shape of a fork,

571
00:40:29.800 --> 00:40:32.800
which rising up into the air would catch it between them,

572
00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:37.800
anything that was about to move in order to keep it still in one single place.

573
00:40:37.800 --> 00:40:41.800
And far away, it seemed to touch the earth.

574
00:40:41.800 --> 00:40:46.800
Afterwards, I found myself inside of myself and I prayed him to locate himself,

575
00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:49.800
and it seemed that he would quite surrender,

576
00:40:49.800 --> 00:40:52.800
so much so that he shared with me the pains of the cross.

577
00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:55.800
Now, what I would say now is merely a suggestion.

578
00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:58.800
I am not claiming it is right.

579
00:40:58.800 --> 00:41:02.800
It looks as if that meteor was guided to a certain spot

580
00:41:02.800 --> 00:41:06.800
where it actually wouldn't do the damage it would have done.

581
00:41:06.800 --> 00:41:09.800
That meteor, if it hit any inhabited place,

582
00:41:09.800 --> 00:41:12.800
it would have killed millions in seconds.

583
00:41:12.800 --> 00:41:16.800
So you see the trunk of the tree and the two branches going up

584
00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:21.800
and making everything still and calm and guiding it down to the earth far away.

585
00:41:21.800 --> 00:41:23.800
Now, far away was the Siberian desert.

586
00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:28.800
Okay, so she's seeing all of this in advance because the Lord gets the victim's soul

587
00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:32.800
to pray in advance so that everything can be helped.

588
00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:37.800
If you're only praying at the time, it's too close to the event.

589
00:41:37.800 --> 00:41:42.800
So November the 13th, 1899, Jesus suffers in seeing us suffer,

590
00:41:42.800 --> 00:41:46.800
us being creatures, and Louisa offers herself to console him.

591
00:41:46.800 --> 00:41:49.800
This morning, my adorable Jesus seemed to be restless.

592
00:41:49.800 --> 00:41:51.800
He'd do nothing but come and go.

593
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:57.800
He'd spend time with me and then almost drawn by his most ardent love for creatures.

594
00:41:57.800 --> 00:42:00.800
He would go and see how they were doing, and with his whole self,

595
00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:02.800
he would suffer with them.

596
00:42:02.800 --> 00:42:05.800
Now, this is a big insight for Louisa and she's going to use it.

597
00:42:05.800 --> 00:42:07.800
Why would he suffer with them?

598
00:42:07.800 --> 00:42:12.800
It's because divine will is inside of every creature, every plant, every tree,

599
00:42:12.800 --> 00:42:16.800
every animal of all levels and in each one of us.

600
00:42:16.800 --> 00:42:19.800
If the divine will wasn't there sustaining our creation,

601
00:42:19.800 --> 00:42:21.800
we would just simply disintegrate.

602
00:42:21.800 --> 00:42:25.800
So he would suffer with them from that which they were suffering,

603
00:42:25.800 --> 00:42:28.800
as if he himself and not they were taken by those sufferings.

604
00:42:28.800 --> 00:42:32.800
Several times I saw the confessor forcing Jesus by means of his priestly authority

605
00:42:32.800 --> 00:42:36.800
to make me suffer his pains so as to be able to placate him.

606
00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:39.800
And while it seemed that he didn't want to be placated,

607
00:42:39.800 --> 00:42:43.800
he would then show himself grateful, tanking wholeheartedly

608
00:42:43.800 --> 00:42:47.800
the one who was occupying himself with holding back his indignant arm.

609
00:42:47.800 --> 00:42:51.800
And so he would share with me one suffering and then another.

610
00:42:51.800 --> 00:42:56.800
Oh, how tender and moving it was to see Jesus in this state.

611
00:42:56.800 --> 00:43:00.800
He would make one's heart split with compassion.

612
00:43:00.800 --> 00:43:04.800
Quite a few times he told me conform to my justice.

613
00:43:04.800 --> 00:43:08.800
For I can take no more, man is too ungrateful,

614
00:43:08.800 --> 00:43:13.800
and he almost forces me from all sides to chastisom.

615
00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:17.800
Now this is only volume three, so I have to remind you where chastisement comes from.

616
00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:22.800
Sin goes up from the earth, but nothing unholy or unworthy can enter the presence of God.

617
00:43:22.800 --> 00:43:26.800
So sin is sent back to us in chastisement.

618
00:43:26.800 --> 00:43:28.800
In other words, we are our own worst enemies.

619
00:43:28.800 --> 00:43:32.800
And depending on what the sin is, the amount of that sin,

620
00:43:32.800 --> 00:43:35.800
the volume, the quantity of it will be the size of the chastisement.

621
00:43:35.800 --> 00:43:40.800
The victim soul moves in between that chastisement and God

622
00:43:40.800 --> 00:43:46.800
and asks the Lord and keeps pleading that the chastisement will be diminished in some way

623
00:43:46.800 --> 00:43:50.800
so that it becomes a lesson but not a judgment for us.

624
00:43:52.800 --> 00:43:57.800
So Jesus said conform to my justice because man is too ungrateful.

625
00:43:57.800 --> 00:44:00.800
And he almost forces me from all sides to chastisement.

626
00:44:00.800 --> 00:44:03.800
He himself snatches the chastisements from my hands.

627
00:44:03.800 --> 00:44:07.800
Jesus said, "If you knew how much I suffer in making use of my justice,

628
00:44:07.800 --> 00:44:11.800
because he is mercy and love, that's his nature.

629
00:44:11.800 --> 00:44:14.800
But it is man himself who uses violence on me.

630
00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:19.800
Had I not done anything other than purchase his freedom at the price of my blood,

631
00:44:19.800 --> 00:44:24.800
he would still have to be grateful to me. But out of greater spite,

632
00:44:24.800 --> 00:44:30.800
he keeps inventing new ways to render my payment that is redemption useless."

633
00:44:30.800 --> 00:44:33.800
So it's unrequited love.

634
00:44:33.800 --> 00:44:36.800
It's a direct insult to Jesus as the Redeemer.

635
00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:40.800
It's flying in the face of God, the Father, our Creator.

636
00:44:40.800 --> 00:44:43.800
And we expect to have no response to this.

637
00:44:43.800 --> 00:44:47.800
But while saying this, Jesus was crying bitterly and to console him,

638
00:44:47.800 --> 00:44:50.800
I said to him, "My sweet God, do not afflict yourself."

639
00:44:50.800 --> 00:44:55.800
I see that your reflection is mostly because you feel forced to chastise the people.

640
00:44:55.800 --> 00:44:57.800
No, this will never be.

641
00:44:57.800 --> 00:45:00.800
If you are all for me, I want to be all for you.

642
00:45:00.800 --> 00:45:02.800
There's a big lesson for all of us.

643
00:45:02.800 --> 00:45:04.800
Notice the all.

644
00:45:04.800 --> 00:45:07.800
And that's Deuteronomy 6, 4 to 10.

645
00:45:07.800 --> 00:45:11.800
You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart and all your soul,

646
00:45:11.800 --> 00:45:14.800
all your mind and all your being.

647
00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:16.800
And love your neighbor as yourself.

648
00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:21.800
So, Louisa said, "If you are all for me, I want to be all for you.

649
00:45:21.800 --> 00:45:24.800
Therefore, you will send the chastisements upon me."

650
00:45:24.800 --> 00:45:26.800
That's what the victim's soul does.

651
00:45:26.800 --> 00:45:27.800
He says, "I'll take the punishment."

652
00:45:27.800 --> 00:45:29.800
Because that was what Jesus did on the cross.

653
00:45:29.800 --> 00:45:32.800
Instead of sending all of us to hell for our sins,

654
00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:35.800
he said, "No, give me the hell, I'll take it."

655
00:45:35.800 --> 00:45:38.800
And we'll give them forgiveness and new life.

656
00:45:38.800 --> 00:45:41.800
So it's unbelievably extraordinary.

657
00:45:41.800 --> 00:45:45.800
So, Louisa said, "You send the chastisements upon me.

658
00:45:45.800 --> 00:45:47.800
Here is the victim.

659
00:45:47.800 --> 00:45:48.800
Always ready.

660
00:45:48.800 --> 00:45:50.800
Here's the victim's soul, we would have to say.

661
00:45:50.800 --> 00:45:52.800
Here is the victim's soul.

662
00:45:52.800 --> 00:45:54.800
Always ready at your disposal.

663
00:45:54.800 --> 00:45:56.800
You can make me suffer whatever you want.

664
00:45:56.800 --> 00:45:59.800
And so your justice will be somehow placated.

665
00:45:59.800 --> 00:46:04.800
And you will be relieved from the affliction you feel in seeing creatures suffer."

666
00:46:04.800 --> 00:46:09.800
Now, beside that, I want you to put Sam 106, verse 23.

667
00:46:09.800 --> 00:46:16.800
The Sam said that if Moses hadn't stood in the breach between God's justice and the sins of the people,

668
00:46:16.800 --> 00:46:19.800
the people would have been wiped out at the time of the Exodus.

669
00:46:19.800 --> 00:46:23.800
So, Louisa continues, "My intention has always been this,

670
00:46:23.800 --> 00:46:29.800
not to conform to justice because if man suffers, you suffer also, more than he does."

671
00:46:29.800 --> 00:46:33.800
As like saying, a parent never enjoys punishing a child.

672
00:46:33.800 --> 00:46:38.800
The parent feels miserable about it, and they feel the punishment more than the kid does.

673
00:46:38.800 --> 00:46:46.800
And so, what Louisa's saying to Jesus is, "It's my love for you that doesn't want you to suffer anymore."

674
00:46:46.800 --> 00:46:50.800
So, she's not saying that human beings are not bad.

675
00:46:50.800 --> 00:46:52.800
She's not saying they're not sinning.

676
00:46:52.800 --> 00:46:54.800
She's admitting all of this.

677
00:46:54.800 --> 00:46:57.800
But she's saying, "I don't want you to suffer."

678
00:46:57.800 --> 00:47:00.800
So, while I was saying this, Louisa said, "Our queen mother came,

679
00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:05.800
and I remembered that I had asked the confessor for the obedience to conform to justice,

680
00:47:05.800 --> 00:47:08.800
that as I had asked the obedience to conform to justice,

681
00:47:08.800 --> 00:47:14.800
he had told me to ask the most holy virgin, whether she wanted me to conform."

682
00:47:14.800 --> 00:47:18.800
And so, I asked her, and she said, "No, no, but pray, my daughter,

683
00:47:18.800 --> 00:47:23.800
that in these days, try as much as you can to keep him with you and to placate him,

684
00:47:23.800 --> 00:47:26.800
because many chastisements have been prepared."

685
00:47:26.800 --> 00:47:30.800
Now, put beside this John chapter 19 verses 26 to 27,

686
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:36.800
because it was at the foot of the cross that blessed mother was constituted mother of all Christians,

687
00:47:36.800 --> 00:47:38.800
mother of all the redeemed.

688
00:47:38.800 --> 00:47:41.800
And she doesn't want her children chastised either.

689
00:47:41.800 --> 00:47:44.800
She wants more and more and more grace to be given to them.

690
00:47:44.800 --> 00:47:47.800
She doesn't want anybody to die in their sins.

691
00:47:47.800 --> 00:47:51.800
So, let's go to November 17, 1899.

692
00:47:51.800 --> 00:47:55.800
Again, we have the priestly authority, and we have the victim's soul.

693
00:47:55.800 --> 00:48:01.800
I'm doing this one as well, because these messages follow on one from the other.

694
00:48:01.800 --> 00:48:04.800
"My beloved Jesus continues to make himself seen all afflicted.

695
00:48:04.800 --> 00:48:07.800
This morning, our queen mother came together with him."

696
00:48:07.800 --> 00:48:13.800
Now, don't forget that the blessed virgin Mary and Jesus were the only ones who lived on this earth

697
00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:17.800
with the divine will from conception to natural death.

698
00:48:17.800 --> 00:48:20.800
He, by nature, because he was God and she by grace.

699
00:48:20.800 --> 00:48:21.800
Okay.

700
00:48:21.800 --> 00:48:29.800
So, here both of them are with her, and Louisa is entering into this wonderful journey of the divine will as well.

701
00:48:29.800 --> 00:48:35.800
So, they came together and it seemed to me that she was bringing him to me so that I would placate him

702
00:48:35.800 --> 00:48:40.800
and pray to him together with her that he would make me suffer to spare the people.

703
00:48:40.800 --> 00:48:44.800
So, I want to give you Isaiah 58 verse 12 there.

704
00:48:44.800 --> 00:48:45.800
Okay.

705
00:48:45.800 --> 00:48:52.800
She told me that if in the past days I had not placed myself in between, that's standing in the breach,

706
00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:54.800
Sam 106 verse 23.

707
00:48:54.800 --> 00:49:01.800
And if the confessor had not used his priestly authority in concurring with his intentions to make me suffer,

708
00:49:01.800 --> 00:49:04.800
many catastrophes would have occurred.

709
00:49:04.800 --> 00:49:07.800
So, blessed mother is telling her, "Your prayer is very powerful.

710
00:49:07.800 --> 00:49:11.800
You have already stopped many chastisements."

711
00:49:11.800 --> 00:49:18.800
In the meantime, Louisa said, "I saw the confessor and immediately I prayed for him to Jesus and to our queen mother."

712
00:49:18.800 --> 00:49:23.800
And Jesus, all kindness, now my book says "Benignity," a word that we don't use anymore.

713
00:49:23.800 --> 00:49:30.800
All kindness said to me, "According to the measure in which he will take care of my interests by praying me

714
00:49:30.800 --> 00:49:36.800
and also by committing himself to renewing his intention in making you suffer in order to spare the people,

715
00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:39.800
so will I take care of him and I'll spare him."

716
00:49:39.800 --> 00:49:47.800
So, Jesus says, "If he wants me to do wonderful things for him, let him do his job of keeping you as a victim's soul

717
00:49:47.800 --> 00:49:49.800
interceding for the people."

718
00:49:49.800 --> 00:49:52.800
He says, "I'll be ready to make this pact with him."

719
00:49:52.800 --> 00:49:58.800
So, after this, Louisa said, "I went about looking at my sweet and only good, and I saw that he was holding two bolts

720
00:49:58.800 --> 00:50:03.800
of lightning in his hands, in one hand, as though he quipped.

721
00:50:03.800 --> 00:50:06.800
He had a strong earthquake and a war."

722
00:50:06.800 --> 00:50:11.800
And in the other, I don't know how you see a war in somebody's hand, but never mind, she saw some kind of an image.

723
00:50:11.800 --> 00:50:14.800
In the other one, many kinds of sudden deaths and contagious diseases.

724
00:50:14.800 --> 00:50:20.800
I began to pray him to pour these bolts of lightning upon me, and I almost wanted to remove them from his hands,

725
00:50:20.800 --> 00:50:24.800
but to prevent me from doing that, he began to move away from me.

726
00:50:24.800 --> 00:50:31.800
I tried to follow him, and so I found myself outside of myself, but Jesus disappeared from me, and I remained alone.

727
00:50:31.800 --> 00:50:40.800
Now, finding myself alone, I went round a little, and I found myself in a place where, in this season, they harvest.

728
00:50:40.800 --> 00:50:47.800
It seemed that the uproar of war were happening there, and I wanted to go and help these poor people,

729
00:50:47.800 --> 00:50:51.800
but the demons prevented me from going there where such things were about to happen,

730
00:50:51.800 --> 00:50:57.800
and they beat me so that I would not be able to help or to prevent their artifices.

731
00:50:57.800 --> 00:51:00.800
They used so much strength as to make me draw back.

732
00:51:00.800 --> 00:51:08.800
Now, Louisa gets a taste all for herself that this is a spiritual war that's going on in the Heavenlies,

733
00:51:08.800 --> 00:51:16.800
and we on earth participate either by our choice for a holy life or our choice for a sinful life,

734
00:51:16.800 --> 00:51:19.800
or either on God's side or on Satan's side.

735
00:51:19.800 --> 00:51:23.800
There is an interesting passage in the book of Daniel, chapter 10, verse 20,

736
00:51:23.800 --> 00:51:29.800
where Daniel had been praying and fasting for, oh, for three weeks, I think it was,

737
00:51:29.800 --> 00:51:33.800
and he said, Lord, why am I getting no result? I can't do any more,

738
00:51:33.800 --> 00:51:38.800
and an angel appeared to him and told him, I think it was Michael the Archangel, yes,

739
00:51:38.800 --> 00:51:41.800
told him I was opposed by the Prince of Persia.

740
00:51:41.800 --> 00:51:45.800
Now, the Prince of Persia, he means a demon, and he said,

741
00:51:45.800 --> 00:51:52.800
I had to fight him for the 21 days that you were fasting in order to be able to come and do what you ask.

742
00:51:52.800 --> 00:51:57.800
Next, terribly important. I'm going to leave that there for now, and we'll pick it up again.
